{"id":"mahabharata-3-188","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":188,"title":"अष्टाशीत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 188 · The signs of the Kali age","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks about the end of the age. Markandeya describes the evils of Kali, when dharma is reversed, castes are confused, rulers plunder, lifespans shrink, and in the end Kalki, a Brahmin born at Shambhala, arises to destroy the barbarians.","kn":"ಯುಗಾಂತದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಧರ್ಮ ತಲೆಕೆಳಗಾಗುವ, ವರ್ಣಸಂಕರವಾಗುವ, ರಾಜರು ಲೂಟಿಮಾಡುವ, ಆಯುಸ್ಸು ಕುಗ್ಗುವ ಕಲಿಯ ದುಷ್ಟತನಗಳನ್ನೂ, ಕೊನೆಗೆ ಶಂಬಲದಲ್ಲಿ ಹುಟ್ಟಿದ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣ ಕಲ್ಕಿ ಮ್ಲೇಚ್ಛರನ್ನು ನಾಶಮಾಡಲು ಉದಿಸುವುದನ್ನೂ ಮಾರ್ಕಂಡೇಯರು ವರ್ಣಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर युग के अन्त के बारे में पूछते हैं। मार्कण्डेय कलि की बुराइयों का वर्णन करते हैं, जब धर्म उलट जाता है, वर्ण मिल जाते हैं, शासक लूटते हैं, आयु घटती है, और अन्त में शम्भल में जन्मा ब्राह्मण कल्कि म्लेच्छों का नाश करने उठता है।","te":"యుగాంతం గురించి యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అడుగుతాడు. ధర్మం తలక్రిందులయ్యే, వర్ణసంకరమయ్యే, పాలకులు దోచుకునే, ఆయుష్షు తగ్గే కలియుగ దుర్లక్షణాలను, చివరకు శంబలంలో పుట్టిన బ్రాహ్మణుడు కల్కి మ్లేచ్ఛులను నాశనం చేయడానికి ఉద్భవించడాన్ని మార్కండేయుడు వర్ణిస్తాడు.","ta":"யுக முடிவு பற்றி யுதிஷ்டிரர் கேட்கிறார். அறம் தலைகீழாகும், வர்ணங்கள் கலக்கும், ஆட்சியாளர்கள் கொள்ளையடிக்கும், ஆயுள் குறையும் கலியின் தீமைகளையும், இறுதியில் ஶம்பலத்தில் பிறந்த அந்தணர் கல்கி ம்லேச்சர்களை அழிக்கத் தோன்றுவதையும் மார்க்கண்டேயர் வர்ணிக்கிறார்.","ml":"യുഗാന്ത്യത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. കലിയുടെ ദോഷങ്ങൾ മാർക്കണ്ഡേയൻ വിവരിക്കുന്നു: ധർമ്മം വിപരീതമാകുന്നു, വർണ്ണങ്ങൾ കലരുന്നു, ഭരണാധികാരികൾ കൊള്ളയടിക്കുന്നു, ആയുസ്സ് കുറയുന്നു. ഒടുവിൽ ശംഭലത്തിൽ ജനിച്ച ബ്രാഹ്മണനായ കൽക്കി, മ്ലേച്ഛരെ നശിപ്പിക്കാനായി ഉദയം ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.188; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्तास्तु ते पार्था यमौ च पुरुषर्षभौ ।\nद्रौपद्या कृष्णया सार्धं नमश्चक्रुर्जनार्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed in this way, the Pandavas and the two twin heroes, together with Draupadi, bowed to Janardana."}},{"n":2,"text":"स चैतान्पुरुषव्याघ्र साम्ना परमवल्गुना ।\nसान्त्वयामास मानार्हान्मन्यमानो यथाविधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Considering them worthy of honour, that tiger among men comforted them with very sweet and gentle words, as was proper."}},{"n":3,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्तु कौन्तेयो मार्कण्डेयं महामुनिम् ।\nपुनः पप्रच्छ साम्राज्ये भविष्यां जगतो गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, asked the great sage Markandeya again about what lay ahead for the world under future rule."}},{"n":4,"text":"आश्चर्यभूतं भवतः श्रुतं नो वदतां वर ।\nमुने भार्गव यद्वृत्तं युगादौ प्रभवाप्ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have told us a marvel, best of speakers, descendant of Bhrigu: what happened at the beginning of the age, and the world's origin and dissolution."}},{"n":5,"text":"अस्मिन्कलियुगेऽप्यस्ति पुनः कौतूहलं मम ।\nसमाकुलेषु धर्मेषु किं नु शेषं भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am still curious about this Kali age too: when dharma is in turmoil, what will remain?"}},{"n":6,"text":"किंवीर्या मानवास्तत्र किमाहारविहारिणः ।\nकिमायुषः किंवसना भविष्यन्ति युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"What strength will people have then, what food and pastimes, what lifespan and clothing, as the age runs out?"}},{"n":7,"text":"कां च काष्ठां समासाद्य पुनः संपत्स्यते कृतम् ।\nविस्तरेण मुने ब्रूहि विचित्राणीह भाषसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"What state will be reached before the Krita age returns? Tell it in detail, sage, for you speak of wonders."}},{"n":8,"text":"इत्युक्तः स मुनिश्रेष्ठः पुनरेवाभ्यभाषत ।\nरमयन्वृष्णिशार्दूलं पाण्डवांश्च महामुनिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to in this way, the best of sages spoke again, delighting the tiger of the Vrishnis and the Pandavas."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"भविष्यं सर्वलोकस्य वृत्तान्तं भरतर्षभ ।\nकलुषं कालमासाद्य कथ्यमानं निबोध मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Listen to me as I tell of the future of the whole world, best of the Bharatas, when it reaches the corrupt age."}},{"n":10,"text":"कृते चतुष्पात्सकलो निर्व्याजोपाधिवर्जितः ।\nवृषः प्रतिष्ठितो धर्मो मनुष्येष्वभवत्पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the Krita age dharma stood on all four feet, a bull, whole and free of any deceit or pretext, among people long ago."}},{"n":11,"text":"अधर्मपादविद्धस्तु त्रिभिरंशैः प्रतिष्ठितः ।\nत्रेतायां द्वापरेऽर्धेन व्यामिश्रो धर्म उच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then unrighteousness struck one foot, so dharma stood on three parts in the Treta and on half in the Dvapara, and is called mixed."}},{"n":12,"text":"त्रिभिरंशैरधर्मस्तु लोकानाक्रम्य तिष्ठति ।\nचतुर्थांशेन धर्मस्तु मनुष्यानुपतिष्ठति ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the Kali age unrighteousness holds the world with three parts, while dharma stays with people only by a fourth."}},{"n":13,"text":"आयुर्वीर्यमथो बुद्धिर्बलं तेजश्च पाण्डव ।\nमनुष्याणामनुयुगं ह्रसतीति निबोध मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lifespan, strength, intelligence, force and radiance, son of Pandu, shrink for people with each age; learn this from me."}},{"n":14,"text":"राजानो ब्राह्मणा वैश्याः शूद्राश्चैव युधिष्ठिर ।\nव्याजैर्धर्मं चरिष्यन्ति धर्मवैतंसिका नराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings, brahmins, merchants and servants, Yudhishthira, will practise dharma through pretence, wearing it as a mere ornament."}},{"n":15,"text":"सत्यं संक्षेप्स्यते लोके नरैः पण्डितमानिभिः ।\nसत्यहान्या ततस्तेषामायुरल्पं भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men who think themselves learned will cut down truth in the world, and by losing truth their lives will become short."}},{"n":16,"text":"आयुषः प्रक्षयाद्विद्यां न शक्ष्यन्त्युपशिक्षितुम् ।\nविद्याहीनानविज्ञानाल्लोभोऽप्यभिभविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"With life cut short they will not be able to learn knowledge, and without learning and understanding, greed will overpower them."}},{"n":17,"text":"लोभक्रोधपरा मूढाः कामसक्ताश्च मानवाः ।\nवैरबद्धा भविष्यन्ति परस्परवधेप्सवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deluded people given to greed and anger, attached to desire, bound by enmity, will want to kill one another."}},{"n":18,"text":"ब्राह्मणाः क्षत्रिया वैश्याः संकीर्यन्तः परस्परम् ।\nशूद्रतुल्या भविष्यन्ति तपःसत्यविवर्जिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins, warriors and merchants will mix with each other, lacking austerity and truth, and will be like servants."}},{"n":19,"text":"अन्त्या मध्या भविष्यन्ति मध्याश्चान्तावसायिनः ।\nईदृशो भविता लोको युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lowest will become middle and the middle will become the lowest; such will the world be when the end of the age arrives."}},{"n":20,"text":"वस्त्राणां प्रवरा शाणी धान्यानां कोरदूषकाः ।\nभार्यामित्राश्च पुरुषा भविष्यन्ति युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the age's end the best clothing will be coarse hemp and the best grain the poor kodo millet, and men will have their wives as their friends."}},{"n":21,"text":"मत्स्यामिषेण जीवन्तो दुहन्तश्चाप्यजैडकम् ।\nगोषु नष्टासु पुरुषा भविष्यन्ति युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Living on fish meat and milking goats and sheep, men will be so when the cows are lost at the end of the age."}},{"n":22,"text":"अन्योन्यं परिमुष्णन्तो हिंसयन्तश्च मानवाः ।\nअजपा नास्तिकाः स्तेना भविष्यन्ति युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Robbing and harming one another, people will be non-chanting atheists and thieves at the age's end."}},{"n":23,"text":"सरित्तीरेषु कुद्दालैर्वापयिष्यन्ति चौषधीः ।\nताश्चाप्यल्पफलास्तेषां भविष्यन्ति युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"They will sow herbs on riverbanks with hoes, and even these will give them little fruit at the end of the age."}},{"n":24,"text":"श्राद्धे दैवे च पुरुषा ये च नित्यं धृतव्रताः ।\nतेऽपि लोभसमायुक्ता भोक्ष्यन्तीह परस्परम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even men who always keep vows in the rites for ancestors and gods will be gripped by greed and eat from one another's share."}},{"n":25,"text":"पिता पुत्रस्य भोक्ता च पितुः पुत्रस्तथैव च ।\nअतिक्रान्तानि भोज्यानि भविष्यन्ति युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Father will eat from the son and son from the father; the old rules about what may be eaten will be overstepped at the age's end."}},{"n":26,"text":"न व्रतानि चरिष्यन्ति ब्राह्मणा वेदनिन्दकाः ।\nन यक्ष्यन्ति न होष्यन्ति हेतुवादविलोभिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins who revile the Veda will not keep vows, nor sacrifice nor offer oblations, lured away by dry argument."}},{"n":27,"text":"निम्ने कृषिं करिष्यन्ति योक्ष्यन्ति धुरि धेनुकाः ।\nएकहायनवत्सांश्च वाहयिष्यन्ति मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They will farm on low ground, yoke milch cows to the plough, and make year-old calves haul loads."}},{"n":28,"text":"पुत्रः पितृवधं कृत्वा पिता पुत्रवधं तथा ।\nनिरुद्वेगो बृहद्वादी न निन्दामुपलप्स्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A son who has killed his father, or a father who has killed his son, will talk big, feel no alarm and incur no blame."}},{"n":29,"text":"म्लेच्छभूतं जगत्सर्वं निष्क्रियं यज्ञवर्जितम् ।\nभविष्यति निरानन्दमनुत्सवमथो तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whole world will become like barbarians, inactive and without sacrifice, joyless and without festivals."}},{"n":30,"text":"प्रायशः कृपणानां हि तथा बन्धुमतामपि ।\nविधवानां च वित्तानि हरिष्यन्तीह मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the most part men will seize the wealth of the poor, of those with kin, and of widows."}},{"n":31,"text":"अल्पवीर्यबलाः स्तब्धा लोभमोहपरायणाः ।\nतत्कथादानसंतुष्टा दुष्टानामपि मानवाः ।\nपरिग्रहं करिष्यन्ति पापाचारपरिग्रहाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Weak and powerless, stubborn, given to greed and delusion, content with tales of the wicked and gifts from them, people of sinful conduct will take and accept what is not theirs."}},{"n":32,"text":"संघातयन्तः कौन्तेय राजानः पापबुद्धयः ।\nपरस्परवधोद्युक्ता मूर्खाः पण्डितमानिनः ।\nभविष्यन्ति युगस्यान्ते क्षत्रिया लोककण्टकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings, son of Kunti, evil in mind, bent on killing one another, foolish yet thinking themselves wise, will be thorns to the world, those warriors at the end of the age."}},{"n":33,"text":"अरक्षितारो लुब्धाश्च मानाहंकारदर्पिताः ।\nकेवलं दण्डरुचयो भविष्यन्ति युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Failing to protect, greedy, swollen with pride and ego, they will love only the rod of punishment at the end of the age."}},{"n":34,"text":"आक्रम्याक्रम्य साधूनां दारांश्चैव धनानि च ।\nभोक्ष्यन्ते निरनुक्रोशा रुदतामपि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Descending again and again on the wives and wealth of the good, pitiless, they will enjoy them even as the victims weep, Bharata."}},{"n":35,"text":"न कन्यां याचते कश्चिन्नापि कन्या प्रदीयते ।\nस्वयंग्राहा भविष्यन्ति युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one will ask for a girl and none will be given in marriage; as the age ends, people will take brides by themselves."}},{"n":36,"text":"राजानश्चाप्यसंतुष्टाः परार्थान्मूढचेतसः ।\nसर्वोपायैर्हरिष्यन्ति युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings, discontented and foolish-minded, will seize others' property by every means as the age closes in."}},{"n":37,"text":"म्लेच्छीभूतं जगत्सर्वं भविष्यति च भारत ।\nहस्तो हस्तं परिमुषेद्युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whole world will become barbarian, Bharata, and hand will rob hand as the age closes in."}},{"n":38,"text":"सत्यं संक्षिप्यते लोके नरैः पण्डितमानिभिः ।\nस्थविरा बालमतयो बालाः स्थविरबुद्धयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men who think themselves learned will cut down truth in the world; the old will have the minds of children and children the wisdom of elders."}},{"n":39,"text":"भीरवः शूरमानीनः शूरा भीरुविषादिनः ।\nन विश्वसन्ति चान्योन्यं युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cowards will pose as heroes and heroes will fall into dejection like cowards; none will trust another as the age closes in."}},{"n":40,"text":"एकाहार्यं जगत्सर्वं लोभमोहव्यवस्थितम् ।\nअधर्मो वर्धति महान्न च धर्मः प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whole world will live on a single meal, fixed in greed and delusion; great unrighteousness will grow and dharma will not go on."}},{"n":41,"text":"ब्राह्मणाः क्षत्रिया वैश्या न शिष्यन्ति जनाधिप ।\nएकवर्णस्तदा लोको भविष्यति युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins, warriors and merchants, lord of men, will not remain distinct; the world will be of one class at the end of the age."}},{"n":42,"text":"न क्षंस्यति पिता पुत्रं पुत्रश्च पितरं तथा ।\nभार्या च पतिशुश्रूषां न करिष्यति काचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"A father will not forgive his son nor a son his father, and no wife will serve her husband."}},{"n":43,"text":"ये यवान्ना जनपदा गोधूमान्नास्तथैव च ।\nतान्देशान्संश्रयिष्यन्ति युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Regions whose people eat barley, and likewise those that eat wheat, are the lands people will resort to as the age closes in."}},{"n":44,"text":"स्वैराहाराश्च पुरुषा योषितश्च विशां पते ।\nअन्योन्यं न सहिष्यन्ति युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men and women, lord of the people, will eat as they please and will not tolerate one another as the age closes in."}},{"n":45,"text":"म्लेच्छभूतं जगत्सर्वं भविष्यति युधिष्ठिर ।\nन श्राद्धैर्हि पितॄंश्चापि तर्पयिष्यन्ति मानवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whole world will become barbarian, Yudhishthira, and people will not satisfy their ancestors with the shraddha rites."}},{"n":46,"text":"न कश्चित्कस्यचिच्छ्रोता न कश्चित्कस्यचिद्गुरुः ।\nतमोग्रस्तस्तदा लोको भविष्यति नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one will listen to anyone and no one will be anyone's teacher; the world will be swallowed in darkness, lord of men."}},{"n":47,"text":"परमायुश्च भविता तदा वर्षाणि षोडश ।\nततः प्राणान्विमोक्ष्यन्ति युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The longest life will then be sixteen years, and people will give up their lives after that, as the age closes in."}},{"n":48,"text":"पञ्चमे वाथ षष्ठे वा वर्षे कन्या प्रसूयते ।\nसप्तवर्षाष्टवर्षाश्च प्रजास्यन्ति नरास्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A girl will bear a child in her fifth or sixth year, and men will beget children at seven or eight."}},{"n":49,"text":"पत्यौ स्त्री तु तदा राजन्पुरुषो वा स्त्रियं प्रति ।\nयुगान्ते राजशार्दूल न तोषमुपयास्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, wife toward husband and man toward wife, tiger among kings, will find no contentment at the age's end."}},{"n":50,"text":"अल्पद्रव्या वृथालिङ्गा हिंसा च प्रभविष्यति ।\nन कश्चित्कस्यचिद्दाता भविष्यति युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wealth will be small, outward marks of religion will be empty, and violence will grow; no one will give to anyone as the age dwindles."}},{"n":51,"text":"अट्टशूला जनपदाः शिवशूलाश्चतुष्पथाः ।\nकेशशूलाः स्त्रियश्चापि भविष्यन्ति युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lands will bristle with spikes of trade, crossroads with Shiva-shrines, and women with spikes of hair, as the age wanes."}},{"n":52,"text":"म्लेच्छाः क्रूराः सर्वभक्षा दारुणाः सर्वकर्मसु ।\nभाविनः पश्चिमे काले मनुष्या नात्र संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Barbarians, cruel, omnivorous and fierce in all their deeds, will be the people of the last age; there is no doubt."}},{"n":53,"text":"क्रयविक्रयकाले च सर्वः सर्वस्य वञ्चनम् ।\nयुगान्ते भरतश्रेष्ठ वृत्तिलोभात्करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"At buying and selling, everyone will cheat everyone, best of the Bharatas, out of greed for livelihood at the age's end."}},{"n":54,"text":"ज्ञानानि चाप्यविज्ञाय करिष्यन्ति क्रियास्तथा ।\nआत्मच्छन्देन वर्तन्ते युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"They will perform rites without understanding the knowledge behind them, and act as self-will directs as the age closes in."}},{"n":55,"text":"स्वभावात्क्रूरकर्माणश्चान्योन्यमभिशङ्किनः ।\nभवितारो जनाः सर्वे संप्राप्ते युगसंक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cruel by nature and suspicious of one another, all people will be so when the age's end comes."}},{"n":56,"text":"आरामांश्चैव वृक्षांश्च नाशयिष्यन्ति निर्व्यथाः ।\nभविता संक्षयो लोके जीवितस्य च देहिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They will ruthlessly destroy gardens and trees, and the lives of embodied beings will shrink in the world."}},{"n":57,"text":"तथा लोभाभिभूताश्च चरिष्यन्ति महीमिमाम् ।\nब्राह्मणाश्च भविष्यन्ति ब्रह्मस्वानि च भुञ्जते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Overcome by greed they will roam this earth, and brahmins will live on property that belongs to brahmins."}},{"n":58,"text":"हाहाकृता द्विजाश्चैव भयार्ता वृषलार्दिताः ।\nत्रातारमलभन्तो वै भ्रमिष्यन्ति महीमिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins crying \"alas\", terrified and oppressed by low-born men, finding no protector, will wander this earth."}},{"n":59,"text":"जीवितान्तकरा रौद्राः क्रूराः प्राणिविहिंसकाः ।\nयदा भविष्यन्ति नरास्तदा संक्षेप्स्यते युगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When men become dreadful, cruel and killers of living things, ending lives, then the age will be cut short."}},{"n":60,"text":"आश्रयिष्यन्ति च नदीः पर्वतान्विषमाणि च ।\nप्रधावमाना वित्रस्ता द्विजाः कुरुकुलोद्वह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmins fleeing in panic will take refuge by rivers, mountains and rough places, bearer of the Kuru line."}},{"n":61,"text":"दस्युप्रपीडिता राजन्काका इव द्विजोत्तमाः ।\nकुराजभिश्च सततं करभारप्रपीडिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pressed by robbers, king, the best of brahmins will be like crows, and ever crushed by the tax burdens of bad kings."}},{"n":62,"text":"धैर्यं त्यक्त्वा महीपाल दारुणे युगसंक्षये ।\nविकर्माणि करिष्यन्ति शूद्राणां परिचारकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving up steadiness at the terrible end of the age, servants of servants will do forbidden deeds, lord of the earth."}},{"n":63,"text":"शूद्रा धर्मं प्रवक्ष्यन्ति ब्राह्मणाः पर्युपासकाः ।\nश्रोतारश्च भविष्यन्ति प्रामाण्येन व्यवस्थिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Servants will teach dharma while brahmins sit near them as attendants and listeners, relying on them as authority."}},{"n":64,"text":"विपरीतश्च लोकोऽयं भविष्यत्यधरोत्तरः ।\nएडूकान्पूजयिष्यन्ति वर्जयिष्यन्ति देवताः ।\nशूद्राः परिचरिष्यन्ति न द्विजान्युगसंक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"This world will be turned upside down; they will worship sheep-shrines and shun the gods, and servants will not serve brahmins at the age's end."}},{"n":65,"text":"आश्रमेषु महर्षीणां ब्राह्मणावसथेषु च ।\nदेवस्थानेषु चैत्येषु नागानामालयेषु च ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the hermitages of the great seers, in brahmins' dwellings, in temples, sacred trees and the abodes of the serpents,"}},{"n":66,"text":"एडूकचिह्ना पृथिवी न देवगृहभूषिता ।\nभविष्यति युगे क्षीणे तद्युगान्तस्य लक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"the earth will be marked with sheep-shrines and not adorned with houses of the gods; this will be the sign of the age's end when the age wanes."}},{"n":67,"text":"यदा रौद्रा धर्महीना मांसादाः पानपास्तथा ।\nभविष्यन्ति नरा नित्यं तदा संक्षेप्स्यते युगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When people become fierce, devoid of dharma, meat-eaters and drinkers always, then the age will be cut short."}},{"n":68,"text":"पुष्पे पुष्पं यदा राजन्फले फलमुपाश्रितम् ।\nप्रजास्यति महाराज तदा संक्षेप्स्यते युगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When flower rests on flower and fruit on fruit, great king, and the plants bear thus, then the age will be cut short."}},{"n":69,"text":"अकालवर्षी पर्जन्यो भविष्यति गते युगे ।\nअक्रमेण मनुष्याणां भविष्यति तदा क्रिया ।\nविरोधमथ यास्यन्ति वृषला ब्राह्मणैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rain-cloud will pour out of season when the age has gone, and people's rites will be out of order; low-born men will turn against brahmins."}},{"n":70,"text":"मही म्लेच्छसमाकीर्णा भविष्यति ततोऽचिरात् ।\nकरभारभयाद्विप्रा भजिष्यन्ति दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Soon the earth will be thronged with barbarians; from fear of taxes, brahmins will scatter in all ten directions."}},{"n":71,"text":"निर्विशेषा जनपदा नरावृष्टिभिरर्दिताः ।\nआश्रमानभिपत्स्यन्ति फलमूलोपजीविनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Regions will be without distinction, afflicted by men and by rains, and people living on roots and fruit will resort to hermitages."}},{"n":72,"text":"एवं पर्याकुले लोके मर्यादा न भविष्यति ।\nन स्थास्यन्त्युपदेशे च शिष्या विप्रियकारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the world is in such chaos there will be no restraint; pupils will not stay by instruction and will act to displease."}},{"n":73,"text":"आचार्योपनिधिश्चैव वत्स्यते तदनन्तरम् ।\nअर्थयुक्त्या प्रवत्स्यन्ति मित्रसंबन्धिबान्धवाः ।\nअभावः सर्वभूतानां युगान्ते च भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then deposits left with the teacher will be forgotten; friends, in-laws and kin will deal with one another only for gain; and at the age's end all beings will vanish."}},{"n":74,"text":"दिशः प्रज्वलिताः सर्वा नक्षत्राणि चलानि च ।\nज्योतींषि प्रतिकूलानि वाताः पर्याकुलास्तथा ।\nउल्कापाताश्च बहवो महाभयनिदर्शकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All directions will blaze, the stars will wander, the lights will turn adverse and the winds will be wild; many meteors will fall, signs of great fear."}},{"n":75,"text":"षड्भिरन्यैश्च सहितो भास्करः प्रतपिष्यति ।\nतुमुलाश्चापि निर्ह्रादा दिग्दाहाश्चापि सर्वशः ।\nकबन्धान्तर्हितो भानुरुदयास्तमये तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sun will burn together with six others; there will be tumultuous roars and fires on all horizons; the sun, hidden by headless forms, will rise and set so."}},{"n":76,"text":"अकालवर्षी च तदा भविष्यति सहस्रदृक् ।\nसस्यानि च न रोक्ष्यन्ति युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The thousand-eyed Indra will then rain out of season, and crops will not grow as the age closes in."}},{"n":77,"text":"अभीक्ष्णं क्रूरवादिन्यः परुषा रुदितप्रियाः ।\nभर्तॄणां वचने चैव न स्थास्यन्ति तदा स्त्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Women will be constantly harsh-tongued, rough and fond of weeping, and will not stand by their husbands' words."}},{"n":78,"text":"पुत्राश्च मातापितरौ हनिष्यन्ति युगक्षये ।\nसूदयिष्यन्ति च पतीन्स्त्रियः पुत्रानपाश्रिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the age's end sons will kill their mothers and fathers, and women, with no support from their sons, will do away with their husbands."}},{"n":79,"text":"अपर्वणि महाराज सूर्यं राहुरुपैष्यति ।\nयुगान्ते हुतभुक्चापि सर्वतः प्रज्वलिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rahu will approach the sun out of season, great king, and fire will blaze everywhere at the age's end."}},{"n":80,"text":"पानीयं भोजनं चैव याचमानास्तदाध्वगाः ।\nन लप्स्यन्ते निवासं च निरस्ताः पथि शेरते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Travellers begging for water and food will get neither nor shelter, and, driven away, will lie down on the road."}},{"n":81,"text":"निर्घातवायसा नागाः शकुनाः समृगद्विजाः ।\nरूक्षा वाचो विमोक्ष्यन्ति युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Crows of ill omen, serpents, birds, beasts and fowl will utter harsh cries as the age closes in."}},{"n":82,"text":"मित्रसंबन्धिनश्चापि संत्यक्ष्यन्ति नरास्तदा ।\nजनं परिजनं चापि युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"People will abandon friends and relatives, their own folk and servants, as the age closes in."}},{"n":83,"text":"अथ देशान्दिशश्चापि पत्तनानि पुराणि च ।\nक्रमशः संश्रयिष्यन्ति युगान्ते पर्युपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"They will go one after another from country to country, direction to direction, town to town and city to city, as the age closes in."}},{"n":84,"text":"हा तात हा सुतेत्येवं तदा वाचः सुदारुणाः ।\nविक्रोशमानश्चान्योन्यं जनो गां पर्यटिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cries of \"Alas, father! Alas, son!\" and other dreadful words will be heard, and people will wander the earth shrieking at one another."}},{"n":85,"text":"ततस्तुमुलसंघाते वर्तमाने युगक्षये ।\nद्विजातिपूर्वको लोकः क्रमेण प्रभविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with that tumult and clash going on as the age wanes, the world, with the twice-born foremost, will gradually arise again."}},{"n":86,"text":"ततः कालान्तरेऽन्यस्मिन्पुनर्लोकविवृद्धये ।\nभविष्यति पुनर्दैवमनुकूलं यदृच्छया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Later, after some time, for the growth of the world, fortune will by chance turn favourable again."}},{"n":87,"text":"यदा चन्द्रश्च सूर्यश्च तथा तिष्यबृहस्पती ।\nएकराशौ समेष्यन्ति प्रपत्स्यति तदा कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the moon, the sun, Tishya and Brihaspati come together in one sign, then the Krita age will arrive."}},{"n":88,"text":"कालवर्षी च पर्जन्यो नक्षत्राणि शुभानि च ।\nप्रदक्षिणा ग्रहाश्चापि भविष्यन्त्यनुलोमगाः ।\nक्षेमं सुभिक्षमारोग्यं भविष्यति निरामयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The rain-cloud will rain in season, the stars will be auspicious, the planets will move rightward and favourably, and there will be safety, plenty and health free of illness."}},{"n":89,"text":"कल्किर्विष्णुयशा नाम द्विजः कालप्रचोदितः ।\nउत्पत्स्यते महावीर्यो महाबुद्धिपराक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A brahmin named Kalki Vishnuyashas, driven by Time, will be born, of great power, great intelligence and prowess."}},{"n":90,"text":"संभूतः संभलग्रामे ब्राह्मणावसथे शुभे ।\nमनसा तस्य सर्वाणि वाहनान्यायुधानि च ।\nउपस्थास्यन्ति योधाश्च शस्त्राणि कवचानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He will be born in the village of Sambhala in a brahmin's auspicious house; at his thought all vehicles and weapons will come to him, and warriors, arms and armour will wait on him."}},{"n":91,"text":"स धर्मविजयी राजा चक्रवर्ती भविष्यति ।\nस चेमं संकुलं लोकं प्रसादमुपनेष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king, conqueror by dharma, will be a universal emperor, and he will bring peace to this troubled world."}},{"n":92,"text":"उत्थितो ब्राह्मणो दीप्तः क्षयान्तकृदुदारधीः ।\nस संक्षेपो हि सर्वस्य युगस्य परिवर्तकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That radiant, high-minded brahmin will rise as the ender of destruction; he will bring the close of everything and turn the age."}},{"n":93,"text":"स सर्वत्र गतान्क्षुद्रान्ब्राह्मणैः परिवारितः ।\nउत्सादयिष्यति तदा सर्वान्म्लेच्छगणान्द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by brahmins, that twice-born will uproot all the mean ones who have spread everywhere and all the hordes of barbarians."}}]}]}